{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Flow step debugger P3 session engine: debug_step(session, mode, pick) moves a debug session (from debug_start) along its recorded TAPE and returns {status, session, mode, cursor, base, length, event, ready, default, ended, depth, running, hash, tape_hash, branches, ...}. Every executed step is recorded with its inverse (a structural change list {p, o, n}), the persistent-global changes, its view and a canonical state hash; a full snapshot every 64 steps; tape capped (50k steps / 4M nodes, oldest 64-blocks dropped). modes: into = one step; over / out = P2 drive's unit rules; run_to = until the next default pick is pick.target {kind: wire|sync|op, index, frame?, case?}; reexecute = one step, forcing execution (forks); continue = to the end on its OWN THREAD (returns at once with running true; pick.budget, default 10000; pick.wait true joins) - stops at breakpoints, pause, budget, or the end; pause = ask a running continue to stop; back (pick.count, default 1) / goto (pick.seq) = roll back or forward without executing, restoring persistent globals (crossed_side_effects lists opaque rust/python command steps passed backwards: rollback restores the interpreter, not the world); edit = set a value at pick.path [\"frames\", i, \"inputs\"|\"results\"|\"out\"|\"args\", ...] to pick.value as an undoable tape step; branch = at a branch's fork point, swap the tape tail with recorded branch pick.id; state = the full view (debug_state). Stepping forward where the tape continues REPLAYS it (replayed counts, nothing executes) while the requested item (pick {kind, index}, or {} = the default) is the one the tape took; another ready item, edit or reexecute FORKS - the old tail is kept as a branch record (max 16). Pick for into/over/out/continue: {} = default, {kind, index} = a READY item (anything else is refused, state unchanged). Mutating modes are refused while a continue runs. Admin-only; no auth checks inside.","import":"use flowlang::command::Command;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\nuse std::panic;","params":[{"name":"session","type":"String"},{"name":"mode","type":"String"},{"name":"pick","type":"JSONObject"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"wojtzq1a16a46b4bcy9f","readers":[],"time":1792887339678,"username":"system","writers":[]}